{"type":"system","subtype":"background_tasks_changed","tasks":[{"task_id":"batt3ijh6","task_type":"local_bash","description":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `balance_aware_heads_alternation_ideal`: people still judge a sequence by how close its switching rate is to their own ideal (person-specific, length-scaled sensitivity, shared penalty for periodic sequences), still favour heads-leaning sequences and still find lopsided H/T counts non-random — but they also notice a streak of identical outcomes as a sign of non-randomness in its own right, so every flip of the longest run beyond two (HHH, HHHH, ...) makes a sequence look less random even when its overall switching rate is the same. The one change is a shared penalty on this absolute excess length of the longest streak, addressing the critique (surviving FDR, q = 0.008) that among pairs with equal switch counts people pick the sequence with the shorter longest run far more often than the incumbent predicts.\nEOF\necho streak_aware_balanced_alternation_ideal > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/balance_aware_heads_alternation_ideal.py\").read()\ndoc='''\"\"\"Streak-aware balanced heads-default alternation ideal.\n\nRefinement of `balance_aware_heads_alternation_ideal`: people judge a sequence\nby how close its switching rate is to their own ideal (person-specific,\nlength-scaled sensitivity; shared periodicity penalty), favour heads-leaning\nsequences and dislike lopsided H/T counts, and they also treat a streak of\nidentical outcomes as a sign of non-randomness: every flip of the longest run\nbeyond two counts against a sequence. The one change is the shared streak\nweight `kappa` on the absolute excess length of the longest run.\n\"\"\"'''\ni=src.index('import numpy')\nsrc=doc+\"\\n\"+src[i:]\nsrc=src.replace('''    def heads_excess(seq):''','''    def streak_excess(seq):\n        longest = run = 1\n        for x, y in zip(seq, seq[1:]):\n            run = run + 1 if x == y else 1\n            longest = max(longest, run)\n        return float(max(0, longest - 2))\n\n    def heads_excess(seq):''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        \"log_trans\":''','''        # Excess longest-run length: b minus a (positive favours a).\n        \"streak_excess_diff_ba\": streak_excess(b) - streak_excess(a),\n        \"log_trans\":''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    log_trans = pm.Data(''','''    streak_diff = pm.Data(\"streak_excess_diff_ba\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    log_trans = pm.Data(''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    theta = ideal''','''    # Streak weight (positive: longer streaks look less random).\n    kappa = pm.Normal(\"kappa\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n\n    theta = ideal''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        + eta * imb_diff\n''','''        + eta * imb_diff\n        + kappa * streak_diff\n''')\nopen(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"}],"uuid":"2cf20166-5007-4639-9657-94c2ec995cf5","session_id":"bb92f407-fad4-4a39-96ba-8f66d369ec20"}
